<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch unemployment seen slightly lower.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch unemployment seen slightly lower.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters expect average Dutch unemployment for the three months to December to be slightly lower than in the three months to November.</p>
<p>The figures are due on Thursday morning. Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p> GMT   Date  Period   Indicator	   Consensus  Range    Prev</p>
<p> 0830  16/1  Oct-Dec  Unemployment NSA  428,000    421-435  431</p>
<p> 0830  16/1  Oct-Dec  Unemployment SA   428,000    422-435  432</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, Generale Bank, MeesPierson, J.P. Morgan, NIBStrating and Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
